  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community is individuals who are politically motivated, particularly those with anti-Hillary Clinton sentiment, and who are receptive to inflammatory, hateful, and misogynistic rhetoric. The meme is designed to incite outrage and delegitimize Hillary Clinton by leveraging extreme criminal imagery (Jeffrey Dahmer) and misogynistic tropes (associating women with hidden corruption and moral failure). The audience likely includes supporters of political opponents who are engaged in smear campaigns, and may be drawn to the meme’s sensationalism and shock value. The use of the phrase 'skeletons in the closet' combined with the violent comparison to Dahmer appeals to those who value moral absolutism and are willing to accept hyperbolic, unverified claims to attack a public figure’s character. The meme’s toxicity and hateful intent suggest it targets communities that are already predisposed to political polarization and the use of degrading, violent metaphors to discredit opponents.",
